    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.51,
      "end_seconds": 23.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.1,
      "text": "doctor I've come along because I know the history if it helps it's cramping pain in the lower tummy doctor he didn't want to come but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.64,
      "end_seconds": 34.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.32,
      "end_seconds": 45.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "I notice it more with certain foods and stress. Honestly, every other day. It feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.63,
      "end_seconds": 52.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "so, what about bloating, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.23,
      "end_seconds": 55.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Yes for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.27,
      "end_seconds": 56.97,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "yes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.05,
      "end_seconds": 66.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "A feeling of not emptying fully was there, but it's gone away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.31,
      "end_seconds": 69.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "what's your current medication list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 73.87,
      "end_seconds": 77.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "he takes pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.41,
      "end_seconds": 78.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Uh-huh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 78.8,
      "end_seconds": 85.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "He is on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.95,
      "end_seconds": 90.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.33,
      "end_seconds": 97.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Acid reflux for two years. Anxiety for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.97,
      "end_seconds": 105.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Mhm. Yes, acid reflux is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.66,
      "end_seconds": 118.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "what about operations anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.9,
      "end_seconds": 123.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "just my appendix out about eight years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.58,
      "end_seconds": 140.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "so, do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.53,
      "end_seconds": 148.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "no, no allergies to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 148.9,
      "end_seconds": 156.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "hold on, doctor, I think he reacted to codeine once. I'm not certain, though"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.88,
      "end_seconds": 159.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I don't remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.43,
      "end_seconds": 169.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Alright, so so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Is there a family history of anything significant?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.76,
      "end_seconds": 175.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure. My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.45,
      "end_seconds": 179.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Tell me about your work."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.82,
      "end_seconds": 186.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "I'm a software engineer, so I'm at a screen all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.73,
      "end_seconds": 188.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "who do you live with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.64,
      "end_seconds": 194.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "I live with my family, my husband and two kids."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.46,
      "end_seconds": 218.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any night-time diarrhoea, fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.77,
      "end_seconds": 223.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "no I'd have mentioned it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.67,
      "end_seconds": 231.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "did you get anaemia blood in the stool or family history of bowel cancer?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.08,
      "end_seconds": 236.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "no, none of that at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.16,
      "end_seconds": 240.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Okay, has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.48,
      "end_seconds": 244.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.52,
      "end_seconds": 248.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "right, how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.14,
      "end_seconds": 250.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.87,
      "end_seconds": 253.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I'll check your pressure and pulse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.12,
      "end_seconds": 265.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "one second.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.21,
      "end_seconds": 287.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "okay: pulse is 72 beats a minute, temp 36.8 degrees, SpO2 99 percent on room air, blood pressure 110 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.38,
      "end_seconds": 290.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.58,
      "end_seconds": 296.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "let's look at it together in a minute"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.68,
      "end_seconds": 300.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, bear with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.12,
      "end_seconds": 302.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.9,
      "end_seconds": 306.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "alright almost done with this part"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.97,
      "end_seconds": 322.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Soft tummy a bit tender on the left lower side no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.91,
      "end_seconds": 341.7,
      "duration_seconds": 13.79,
      "text": "That's fine sit up. Okay thinking it it through the most likely explanation is irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. I can't rule out coeliac disease yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.86,
      "end_seconds": 345.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is this gonna go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.46,
      "end_seconds": 372.43,
      "duration_seconds": 22.97,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis is my leading thought, not anything worse i think a coeliac test makes sense here, for bloating the result will help us decide whether anything more is needed i'm going to order blood tests, for bowel symptoms"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.82,
      "end_seconds": 375.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.21,
      "end_seconds": 407.41,
      "duration_seconds": 31.2,
      "text": "let's use mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day, for four weeks. You take it by mouth. That should help with abdominal cramps. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. I'd like you back in six weeks. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.03,
      "end_seconds": 420.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "So, uh, I take the mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.78,
      "end_seconds": 425.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Yes exactly right. Call the clinic if you need us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.38,
      "end_seconds": 429.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.62,
      "end_seconds": 432.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "goodbye"
    }
  ]
